<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::maritime_incident_rate" target="energy_chokepoints::chokepoint_security" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising rate of ship seizures, attacks and harassment directly forces temporary closures, naval escorts, and de facto denial-of-transit conditions that reduce the operational openness and safety of maritime chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::maritime_incident_rate" target="energy_chokepoints::tanker_freight_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased incidents raise war‑risk insurance premiums, force rerouting and speed reductions, and reduce available safe sailings, directly lifting tanker hire and voyage rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::maritime_incident_rate" target="global_bond_rate_shock::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in disruptive maritime incidents raises trade and counterparty risk, prompting dealers and market-makers to pull inventory and widen bid-ask spreads, thereby reducing short-term liquidity in global fixed-income markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::maritime_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::munitions_stockpile" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in attacks/seizures on commercial and military shipping in regional routes raises loss and delay rates for Western and Black Sea‑bound arms shipments (including ammunition and missiles), directly reducing the delivered munitions available for operations in the Russia‑Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
