  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp drawdowns in commercial and strategic oil inventories that threaten price spikes prompt sovereigns and central banks (especially in commodity-dependent states) to undertake direct market interventions—reserve releases, FX operations or targeted bond purchases—to stabilize prices and financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
