<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" target="energy_chokepoints::tanker_freight_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased drone attacks on tankers, escorts and port approaches raise insurance and security surcharges and force rerouting or slower transits, pushing up tanker freight rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" target="global_bond_rate_shock::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified drone attacks increase uncertainty about regional assets and counterparty exposures, causing dealers to pull back inventories and widen bid‑ask spreads, reducing short‑term fixed‑income market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" target="iran_regional_escalation::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Visible, high‑intensity drone employment in Ukraine accelerates proliferation of tactics, ready designs and commercial procurement channels that Iran and Iran-linked proxies adopt to harass or strike shipping and offshore infrastructure, raising incidents at sea.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" target="iran_regional_escalation::military_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased drone use and demonstrated effectiveness in Ukraine lowers technical and operational barriers for Iran and its proxies to mount longer‑range, lower‑cost strikes against regional rivals, increasing the frequency of kinetic confrontations.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::safety_incident_frequenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased frontline use and experimentation with AI-guided and improvised drone systems produces more operational failures, unintended behaviors, capture of systems, and leakage of models/data, raising the observed frequency of safety and misuse incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_warfare_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" target="russia_ukraine_war::mil_modernization_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">?</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" target="russia_ukraine_war::intel_surveillance_cover" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" target="energy_chokepoints::chokepoint_security" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Improved integrated air defenses intercept missile and drone threats to ships and port facilities, directly lowering the incidence of successful attacks and increasing transit security through chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::air_defense_capacity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::model_deployment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Deployment of more capable integrated air defenses creates immediate operational demand for AI-driven countermeasures (targeting, EW, decoy/autonomy systems), prompting adversaries and suppliers to deploy new or upgraded models more quickly.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
