<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="energy_chokepoints::oil_spot_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long‑term sovereign yields attract portfolio flows into fixed income and raise the discount rate applied to commodity cash flows, diminishing speculative and carry demand for oil and exerting downward pressure on near‑term spot prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="iran_regional_escalation::oil_gas_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained rises in long‑term sovereign yields signal and help precipitate global demand weakening (through higher financing costs and lower investment), which reduces crude and LNG liftings and contracted volumes exported from the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_funding_flow_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields raises government debt servicing and marginal borrowing costs, forcing near-term budget reprioritization and reducing the rate at which funds are committed and disbursed to military procurement programs.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::model_deployment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in long-term government yields raises the discount rate and long-horizon financing costs for capital- and compute-intensive AI projects, reducing their expected NPV and causing firms to delay or cancel planned model deployments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
