<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::intervention_activity" target="iran_regional_escalation::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Aggressive central‑bank market interventions that stabilize financial markets and preserve bank balance sheets give sanctioning governments and compliance units more operational capacity and political room to sustain or tighten sanctions enforcement in the short term.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::intervention_activity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::national_security_pressu" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">High-profile market interventions (large asset purchases/sales or emergency operations) signal acute financial stress and political exposure, prompting authorities to tighten export controls and investment screening for sensitive tech to shield strategic sectors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
