<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulation_adoption_rate" target="energy_chokepoints::tanker_freight_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Faster adoption of cross-border tech and export regulations induces trade decoupling and sourcing shifts that lengthen average voyage distances and create episodic demand for alternative shipping routes, increasing demand for tanker capacity and lifting freight rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulation_adoption_rate" target="global_bond_rate_shock::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Fast-moving, heterogeneous AI regulations (data localization, licensing, compliance regimes) create operational frictions and legal risk for cross-border trading and custody, causing market makers to scale back activity and reducing short-term bond market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulation_adoption_rate" target="iran_regional_escalation::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid adoption of export controls, compliance rules, and extraterritorial tech regulations forces firms to reroute, withhold, or block shipments and financial flows to avoid legal risk, producing immediate disruptions in logistics for energy and critical components connected to the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
